---
Create an entity

Usage: specforge new [OPTIONS] [KIND] [ID] [TITLE] [FIELDS]...

Arguments:
  [KIND]
          The kind of entity (behavior, invariant, …)

  [ID]
          The new entity's id

  [TITLE]
          The new entity's title

  [FIELDS]...
          The kind's fields: `--<field> <value>`

Options:
      --in <FILE>
          The file, relative to the project root; created when missing

      --field <NAME=VALUE>
          Any field of the kind, by name: `--field path=src/a.rs`; the way to set one named like an option; repeat for several

      --verify <KIND:TEXT>
          A `verify` obligation: `kind:text` when the kind is one of the new kind's verify kinds, else the whole text; repeat for several

      --revision <REVISION>
          The revision of the target file (`sha256:<digest>`, or `absent` for a new file); refused with `stale_revision` when the file has changed since

      --dry-run
          Print the diff and write nothing

  -h, --help
          Print help (with a kind, that kind's field flags)

      --path <PATH>
          A path inside the project (the nearest directory at or above it holding specforge.json; none: the directory itself, with the default configuration)
          
          [default: .]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: human or json
          
          [default: human]
          [possible values: human, json]

The kind's fields are flags too: `specforge new <kind> --help` lists them.
